2bb69f336008bdfa40b022861a6a0bbfe9cbacc2.message:
perf(video): re-check only the cached textures a guest-memory write touched (#63)

Every NV0039 copy bumped one global dirty generation
(rsx_draw_engine_mark_guest_dirty), so the next bind of every cached
texture, in that same frame, repeated the content check it had already
made. That is a sparse hash, and a full hash for small textures.

The engine now records where the writes behind the last 256 generations
landed. A texture already checked this frame is checked again only if one
of the writes since its check overlaps its bytes. Otherwise it takes the
new generation and moves on. These keep the old rule (any write re-checks):
- picture-backed textures;
- textures read through a custom guest reader;
- a texture whose missed writes are older than the ring;
- a ring slot that has been reused.
The once-per-frame check of every texture used in a frame is unchanged, so
bytes changed without a recorded write are still found the next frame, as
before.

test_rsx_draw_engine covers:
- a write elsewhere not re-checking within the frame;
- the next frame still seeing new bytes;
- a write touching only the last byte re-checking;
- a write ending just before the texture not re-checking;
- an overflowed ring re-checking.

