9f85d1178c81d62b046b5e934080a1075bad4317.message:
Notes: EDGE's output contract, mapped from the 120 gate jobs

What a job writes:
- the ring allocation: one atomic line per SPU, two rings, and labels the GPU releases;
- the indices and vertices in the main ring;
- for 22 jobs, a fragment program patched with two constant blocks, in the second ring;
- the hole: a fixed list of RSX methods (vertex layout, the program binding, the viewport
  block, the index array, the draws in 256-index pieces, the semaphore releases), padded
  with NOPs.

Also what a job reads (descriptor, DMA list, streams, blocks), and what is still to map.

c80c9b02d73d6d2136d71310d00584685b60e43b.message:
Notes: an EDGE job's input set, from 160 consecutive jobs

Each capture holds the input set of the job after it on its SPU. The set is a 160-byte job
descriptor (the DMA list's EA, the ring lines, the hole's EA), a DMA list of up to 22 elements,
and the elements, fetched into one of two buffer sets. The elements are:
- the parameter block (sub-blocks of lights);
- the three pieces;
- a control word, the index and vertex streams, the segment header;
- the input and output vertex formats (RSX vertex types, an entry per attribute);
- the frame's viewport block, the local-to-world matrix, and more blocks for lit jobs.

