tests/setup_fetch_check.cpp runs the real PythonFetch (setup_python.cpp with setup_http.cpp and setup_unzip.cpp), with
the data folder and the free space stubbed. Its cases:
- system: curl and tar, as on Windows;
- own: DES_SETUP_NO_SYSTEM_TOOLS=1, so WinHTTP and the host's own unzip, as on Wine and CrossOver;
- resume: own, stopped once the .part file has 2 MB, then started again, which must carry on from the file;
- same: the two folders hold the same files, byte for byte;
- refusals: the zip reader refuses a cut archive and a changed byte, and unpacks the archive as it is.

It is built on demand (cmake --build <build> --target setup_fetch_check), Windows only, and downloads python.org's
embeddable zip three times.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

