646b5daa3d3908ea86599f547cada70e29f4f317.message:
ps3recomp: a level's first frame, the counts the port reads, three diagnostics

The fork's master at d779440 (five commits on 1d5988f):

- staging in the D3D12 and Vulkan engines is a chain of chunks and is
  never read back; D3D12 textures are placed in heaps and its
  vertex-cache buffers are ranges of mapped pages. Chapter 1's first
  frame: 836 -> 206 ms, the walker's draws in it 676 -> 66 ms;
- an object released with records queued outlives them (both engines;
  the Vulkan validation layer found an image destroyed while a queued
  command buffer used it);
- g_rsx_video_plane_uploads and g_rsx_frame_draws, which the next two
  commits read;
- RSX_HITCH_LOG's split of a frame's upload time, D3D12_DBG's messages
  on stderr, PPU_WAITPROF=2's most frequent calls;
- the engines' "first N times" gates stop counting at N.

